  <article class="prose">
    <div class="eyebrow">PERSONAL INDEX · INTERESTS & QUESTIONS</div>
    <h1>Things I Keep Coming Back To</h1>
    <p class="small-note">A personal map of my interests, questions, curiosities and ongoing explorations.</p>

    <p>I often find myself returning to the same subjects. I read about them, search for information, discuss them, start projects around them and sometimes leave them aside for a while, only to come back months later.</p>
    <p>Some are technical. Others are scientific, philosophical, creative or entrepreneurial.</p>
    <p>This page is an attempt to keep track of them.</p>
    <p>It is not a list of things I already know. It is a record of things I want to understand, questions I have not answered and ideas I might want to explore further.</p>

    <h2>1. Engineering, Mechanics and Industrial Systems</h2>
    <p>I keep coming back to how physical systems work, how machines are designed and how industrial processes can be improved.</p>
    <p><strong>Topics I return to:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Mechanical engineering and machine design</li><li>Mechatronics and automation</li><li>Industrial maintenance and reliability</li><li>Failure analysis and root cause analysis</li><li>Materials science and material properties</li><li>Corrosion, coatings and surface engineering</li><li>Manufacturing processes and production systems</li><li>CNC machining and computer-aided manufacturing</li><li>CAD, 3D modelling and finite element analysis</li><li>Metrology, dimensional inspection and reverse engineering</li><li>Welding and non-destructive testing</li><li>Pneumatics, sensors and control systems</li><li>Quality management and continuous improvement</li><li>Sustainable manufacturing and industrial efficiency</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Questions I keep asking:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Why do machines fail?</li><li>How can we predict and prevent failures?</li><li>How do materials behave under different conditions?</li><li>How can manufacturing processes become more efficient?</li><li>How can we design systems that are easier to maintain?</li><li>What makes an industrial system reliable?</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. Robotics, Science and Research</h2>
    <p>I am interested in going beyond using existing technologies and understanding how new ones can be developed.</p>
    <p><strong>Topics I return to:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Robotics and autonomous systems</li><li>Mechanical and electronic integration</li><li>Control theory and automation</li><li>Artificial intelligence in physical systems</li><li>Sensors, perception and machine vision</li><li>Embedded systems and microcontrollers</li><li>Experimental science and scientific methodology</li><li>Reading and analysing research papers</li><li>Mathematical models and simulations</li><li>Developing and testing hypotheses</li><li>Research laboratories and innovation environments</li><li>The relationship between fundamental research and engineering applications</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Questions I keep asking:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>How do we move from a scientific idea to an experiment?</li><li>How are new technologies actually invented?</li><li>What makes a good research environment?</li><li>How can a small team conduct meaningful experiments?</li><li>What could a robotics and innovation laboratory in Togo look like?</li><li>What technologies could be developed locally rather than simply imported?</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Artificial Intelligence, Software and Computing</h2>
    <p>I regularly explore how software and AI can help people think, work, research and build things.</p>
    <p><strong>Topics I return to:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Artificial intelligence and large language models</li><li>AI agents and autonomous workflows</li><li>Python programming</li><li>Databases and data management</li><li>SQLite, SQL and structured information</li><li>Automation with tools such as Make and n8n</li><li>Software development and personal applications</li><li>GitHub and open-source projects</li><li>Data analysis and visualisation</li><li>Digital tools for industrial operations</li><li>Predictive maintenance</li><li>AI-assisted research and writing</li><li>Human-computer interaction</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Projects and ideas:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>SmartMaintenance DB</li><li>Industrial Engineering Lab</li><li>Industrial OS</li><li>AI-assisted industrial problem solving</li><li>Personal knowledge management systems</li><li>Automation of repetitive administrative and business tasks</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Questions I keep asking:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>What can one person build with modern AI tools?</li><li>How can software improve traditional industries?</li><li>How can we turn information into structured, useful data?</li><li>Which tasks should be automated?</li><li>How can AI become a practical engineering tool?</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Learning, Reading and Knowledge Management</h2>
    <p>I repeatedly return to the question of how to learn more effectively and develop a deeper understanding of subjects.</p>
    <p><strong>Topics I return to:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Scientific papers and academic research</li><li>Books, essays and independent blogs</li><li>First-principles thinking</li><li>Critical thinking and reasoning</li><li>Learning difficult technical subjects</li><li>Writing as a tool for thinking</li><li>Note-taking and knowledge management</li><li>Connecting ideas across disciplines</li><li>Building a personal knowledge library</li><li>Intellectual curiosity and independent learning</li><li>The history of scientific and technological discoveries</li><li>How experts develop expertise</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>People and sources I want to revisit:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Naval Ravikant</li><li>Alexey Guzey</li><li>Andrew Zuckerman</li><li>Paul Graham</li><li>Patrick Collison</li><li>Andrej Karpathy</li><li>David Chalmers</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Questions I keep asking:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>How do I know whether I truly understand something?</li><li>How can I remember what I read?</li><li>How do ideas from different fields connect?</li><li>How can writing improve my thinking?</li><li>How do independent researchers choose what to investigate?</li><li>How can I develop original ideas rather than simply repeat existing ones?</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Entrepreneurship, Innovation and Building Things</h2>
    <p>I often think about how to transform knowledge, technical skills and observations into useful products, services and organisations.</p>
    <p><strong>Topics I return to:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Starting businesses with limited resources</li><li>Identifying real problems worth solving</li><li>Product development</li><li>Industrial services</li><li>Prototyping and experimentation</li><li>Business models</li><li>Technology entrepreneurship</li><li>Building small teams</li><li>Finding customers and understanding their needs</li><li>Manufacturing and local production</li><li>Innovation ecosystems</li><li>African industrial development</li><li>Technology transfer and local adaptation</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Projects I want to explore or develop:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Industrial Engineering Lab</li><li>Lomé Industrial Solutions</li><li>A robotics and innovation laboratory in Togo</li><li>Digital maintenance systems for local industries</li><li>CAD, reverse engineering and technical services</li><li>Manufacturing and prototyping capabilities in Togo</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Questions I keep asking:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>How do you identify a problem people will pay to solve?</li><li>How can a technical idea become a viable business?</li><li>What can be built with almost no initial capital?</li><li>How can local industries develop stronger technical capabilities?</li><li>How do you build an organisation that can operate without depending entirely on its founder?</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Togo, Africa and Industrial Development</h2>
    <p>I frequently return to questions about the technological and industrial future of Togo.</p>
    <p><strong>Topics I return to:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Industrialisation in Togo</li><li>Local manufacturing capabilities</li><li>Agro-industrial processing</li><li>Food production and preservation</li><li>Machinery sourcing and maintenance</li><li>Engineering education and technical training</li><li>Robotics education</li><li>Scientific laboratories</li><li>Technology entrepreneurship</li><li>Local supply chains</li><li>Infrastructure and energy</li><li>The relationship between research and economic development</li><li>Adapting technologies to local constraints</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Questions I keep asking:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Why are some products imported when they could potentially be manufactured locally?</li><li>What prevents small industries from becoming more productive?</li><li>What technical skills are missing?</li><li>How can universities, companies and laboratories collaborate?</li><li>What would it take to develop a local robotics ecosystem?</li><li>Which industrial problems should be solved first?</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Philosophy, Consciousness and Human Thinking</h2>
    <p>Beyond technical subjects, I am also interested in understanding the mind, human experience and the assumptions behind our understanding of reality.</p>
    <p><strong>Topics I return to:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Free will and determinism</li><li>Consciousness and subjective experience</li><li>The hard problem of consciousness</li><li>Panpsychism and dualism</li><li>Artificial consciousness</li><li>Philosophy of mind</li><li>Human cognition</li><li>Rationality and decision-making</li><li>Psychology and behavioural science</li><li>Creativity</li><li>The nature of reality</li><li>Ethics and moral status</li><li>Effective altruism</li><li>The relationship between science and philosophy</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Questions I keep asking:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>What is consciousness?</li><li>Could machines ever become conscious?</li><li>How much control do we have over our decisions?</li><li>What makes an experience meaningful?</li><li>How should we reason about things we cannot directly observe?</li><li>What can science tell us about the nature of reality?</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Creativity, Design and Systems</h2>
    <p>I also return to the relationship between technical functionality and beauty. I am interested in creating things that are not only useful but also well-designed.</p>
    <p><strong>Topics I return to:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Industrial design and product design</li><li>Architecture and construction</li><li>Visual systems and minimalism</li><li>Aesthetics and functionality</li><li>Creative problem solving</li><li>Writing and communication</li><li>Building personal digital tools</li><li>Designing better workflows</li><li>The relationship between simplicity and complexity</li>
    </ul>
    <p>A recurring idea: making complex systems easier to understand and use without losing what makes them powerful.</p>

    <h2>9. Personal Development and Long-Term Thinking</h2>
    <p>Some of my questions concern how to organise my own life and make decisions over long periods.</p>
    <p><strong>Topics I return to:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Long-term planning and time management</li><li>Personal productivity and building habits</li><li>Financial independence and investing</li><li>Career development and developing technical expertise</li><li>Physical fitness and strength</li><li>Learning languages</li><li>Building meaningful relationships</li><li>Designing a life around curiosity and creation</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Questions I keep asking:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>What should I spend my time learning?</li><li>Which skills will compound over decades?</li><li>How do I balance studying, working and building projects?</li><li>How can I make progress without constantly changing direction?</li><li>What does a meaningful and well-designed life look like?</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Connections Worth Exploring</h2>
    <p>Some of the most interesting questions emerge where these subjects overlap.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Materials science × Robotics:</strong> How do new materials enable better machines?</li>
      <li><strong>AI × Industrial maintenance:</strong> Can intelligent systems anticipate equipment failures?</li>
      <li><strong>Robotics × Togo:</strong> What can locally developed robotics solve?</li>
      <li><strong>Research × Entrepreneurship:</strong> How can scientific discoveries become useful products?</li>
      <li><strong>Philosophy × AI:</strong> What would it mean for an artificial system to understand something?</li>
      <li><strong>Learning × Engineering:</strong> How do we develop deep technical intuition?</li>
      <li><strong>Industrial design × Manufacturing:</strong> How can products become simpler, more reliable and easier to manufacture?</li>
      <li><strong>Knowledge management × Creativity:</strong> Can organising knowledge help generate original ideas?</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Projects I Keep Thinking About</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Robotics and Innovation Laboratory in Togo — research, robotics and education</li>
      <li>Industrial Engineering Lab — engineering, industry and entrepreneurship</li>
      <li>SmartMaintenance DB — software, maintenance and industrial systems</li>
      <li>Lomé Industrial Solutions — industrial services and manufacturing</li>
      <li>Personal Knowledge Library — learning and research</li>
      <li>Personal website and essays — writing and thinking</li>
      <li>Industrial OS — software, data and operations</li>
      <li>Memento — time, personal systems and design</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>An Open List</h2>
    <p>This page is not meant to be definitive.</p>
    <p>My interests will change. Some subjects will become more important, others may disappear. New questions will emerge from books, conversations, experiments, work and unexpected discoveries.</p>
    <p>I want to keep this page as a reference point.</p>
    <p>A place to return when I do not know what to read next, when I need a new research question, when I want to start a project or when I want to remember what has consistently captured my attention.</p>
    <p>The goal is not to pursue everything at once.</p>
    <p>It is to avoid losing track of the things I keep coming back to.</p>
